      <div type="clause" n="Prol., 1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAs">V As</ref> Prol., 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="166" ed="#liebermann"/>Nu hæbbe ic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.5"/> funden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.6"/> mid ðæm witum, þe mid me wæron æt Eaxanceastre to middanwintre, ðæt þa ealle beon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> gearwe mid him silfum ⁊ mid wife ⁊ mid ærfe ⁊ mid eallum þingum to farenne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/> ðider ic wille — buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> hy ofer þis geswican willan —, on þa gerad þæt hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> næfre eft on eard ne cuman.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="166" ed="#liebermann"/>Nu hæbbe ic funden mid ðæm witum, ðe æt Eaxceastre mid we wæron to middu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>wintre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ða ealle syn gearwe mid hire<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.1"/> sylfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ mid yrfe ⁊ mid wife ⁊ mid eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðingu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> to færenne ðider ðider ic ðonne wille—butan hi ofer ðis geswican willan—, on ða gerade ðe heo næfre eft on eorda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.1"/> ne cumen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Prol., 1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="167" ed="#liebermann"/>Nunc inueni cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.7"/> illis sapientibus, qui apud Exoniam mecum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.8"/> fuerunt in sancto natali Domini, quod parati sunt omnino (quando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.9"/> uelim) cum se ipsis et uxoribus et pecunia et omni re<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.10"/> sua ire quo tunc uolero — nisi malefactores post<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.11"/> hoc cessauerint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.4"/> (conquiescant) —, eo tenore quo nunquam deinceps in patriam istam redeant.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="§1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#attenborough"/>Nu hæbbe ic funden<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.5"/> mid ðæm witum, þe mid me wæron æt Eaxanceastre to middanwintre, ðæt þa ealle beon<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.6"/> gearwe mid him<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.7"/> silfum ⁊ mid wife ⁊ mid ærfe<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.8"/> ⁊ mid eallum þingum to farenne ðider ic wille<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.9"/>—buton<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.10"/> hy ofer þis geswican willan—on þa gerad þæt hy<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.11"/> næfre eft on eard<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.12"/> ne cuman<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.fn.13"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="167" ed="#liebermann"/>Nun habe ich beschlossen mit jenen Witan, die in Exeter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.1"/> zu Weihnachten bei mir waren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.2"/>, dass jene [Friedensstörer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.3"/>] alle für sich selbst und mit Weib und mit Fahrhabe und mit allen Sachen bereit sein sollen, dorthin<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.4"/> auszuwandern, wohin ich will<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.5"/> — es sei denn, sie wollen nach diesem [von Missethat] abstehen —, dergestalt, dass sie niemals wieder in die Heimathgegend<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.6"/> kommen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Now I have decided with those witan who were with me at Exeter at Christmas that those [breakers of the peace] shall all be ready, themselves and with wife and with goods and with all things, to emigrate to wherever I wish — unless they will desist [from wrongdoing] after this —, on the condition that they never come back to the home country.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="153" ed="#attenborough"/>Now I have decided with the councillors who have been<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.1"/> with me at Exeter at midwinter, that all [disturbers of the peace]<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.2"/> shall be ready to go themselves, with their wives, with their property<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.3"/>, and with everything [they possess], whithersoever I wish, unless henceforth they are willing to cease [from wrongdoing]—with the further provision that they never afterwards return to their native district.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="423" ed="#whitelock"/>Now I have concluded, along with the councillors who have been with me at Christmas at Exeter, that all [the disturbers of the peace] are to be ready, themselves, their wives and their cattle and all things, to go whither I wish—unless they are willing to desist after this—on condition that they never come back into their native district.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIAs_6">III As 6</ref>; <ref target="clause:IVAs_3">IV As 3</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eum <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eum K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. m. <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. m. TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. u. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. u. lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rem <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rem Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. h. <hi rend="italic">fehlt TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. h. lacking in TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">167</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lesart Lond; eingeklammert Lesart der übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">reading of Lond before the bracket; in brackets the reading of the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert</hi> gefunden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered gefunden</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">beo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi> [<hi rend="italic">über</hi> sie?]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">beo on an erasure [over sie?]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgen vier bis sechs Buchst. radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">four to six letters erased after it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S.</hi> Einl. 4. Hierauf bezieht sich III As 6, wo der Grund zur folgenden Massregel erhellt: der Staat ist zu schwach, die übermächtigen gesetzbrechenden Sippen in deren Heimat zu bändigen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See</hi> Introduction 4. III As 6 refers to this, and there the reason for the following measure becomes clear: the state is too weak to subdue the overmighty, law-breaking kindreds in their home districts</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht etwa auf ein früheres Gemot spielt der König an, sondern die Urk. fixiert nur das eben Geschehene im Tempus der Vergangenheit, wie in II As viele Sätze <hi rend="italic">we cwædon</hi> beginnen. Ebenso Hl Pro; Wi; Ine; Af El 49, 9 f.; AGu; II Ew. Modern stünde das Präsens dafür. Schmid ward durch Thorpe an dieser Meinung im Texte irre, kehrte aber dann zu ihr S. <hi rend="smallcaps">xlvi</hi> zurück</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The king is not, say, alluding to an earlier gemot; rather, the charter merely records what has just taken place, in the past tense, just as in II As many clauses begin <hi rend="italic">we cwædon</hi>. Likewise Hl Pro; Wi; Ine; Af El 49, 9 f.; AGu; II Ew. In modern usage the present tense would stand instead. Schmid was misled by Thorpe into doubting this view in his text, but then returned to it on p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xlvi</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Ellipse wird verständlich durch III 6. IV 3. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Verpflanzung 1. a. — Q scheint durch Verkennung des Subjekts das Fortziehen auf die Witan zu deuten, vermutlich zur Verfolgung der Friedbrecher: aber was soll beim Strafvollzuge Weib und Fahrhabe?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The ellipsis becomes intelligible from III 6. IV 3. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Verpflanzung 1. a. — Q, by mistaking the subject, seems to refer the moving away to the witan, presumably in pursuit of the breakers of the peace: but what would wife and chattels have to do with the execution of punishment?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">þider þider</hi> ist ursprünglich; das erste nur durch H cor fortradiert. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> <hi rend="italic">fundiað þider þider his eard is;</hi> Ælfred <hi rend="italic">Boethius</hi> 34, 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">þider þider</hi> is original; the first is carried on in the tradition only by H cor. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> <hi rend="italic">fundiað þider þider his eard is;</hi> Ælfred <hi rend="italic">Boethius</hi> 34, 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q denkt mit Unrecht an Verbannung aus England</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q wrongly thinks of banishment from England</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Land’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb: eard</hi> 3. 4, und bei Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>: ‘Landesteil, Wohnplatz, Heimatbezirk’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘land’; cf. <hi rend="italic">Wb: eard</hi> 3. 4, and in Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi>: ‘part of a country, dwelling-place, home district’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Or, perhaps, ‘are with me,’ if, as seems probable, this meeting was being held at the time when the laws were promulgated (Liebermann).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Implied in the previous section (cf. III As. cap. 6; IV As. cap. 3).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAs_Prol-to-1.attnote.n.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Perhaps ‘cattle’ (cf. cap. 2, below, etc.).</seg></note>
